PacketDemodFramer::PACKETDEMOD_CHASE_MAX is declared as a static const int with
an in-class initialiser and never defined out of line. chaseDecode() passes it to
std::min(), which takes its arguments by const reference and so odr-uses it. In
C++17 a static const (as opposed to static constexpr) data member is not
implicitly inline, so the compiler emits a reference to a symbol nothing defines
and libdemodpacket.so fails to load at runtime:

  PluginManager::loadPluginsDir: Cannot load library libdemodpacket.so:
  undefined symbol: _ZN17PacketDemodFramer21PACKETDEMOD_CHASE_MAXE

The Packet demodulator is then silently missing from the channel list, and the
bundled "ISS Packet" example configuration loads without its demodulator.

Making the member constexpr makes it implicitly inline in C++17, which gives it
the definition std::min needs. Reported upstream behaviour, not Gentoo-specific.

--- a/plugins/channelrx/demodpacket/packetdemodframer.h	2026-08-19 12:28:39.000000000 -0600
+++ b/plugins/channelrx/demodpacket/packetdemodframer.h	2026-09-21 11:53:38.480661645 -0600
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
     // and re-CRC'd frames for every CRC failure on every detector, so 12 is already 4095;
     // the value reaches here from presets and the REST API, neither of which bounds it,
     // and 1u << n is undefined once n reaches 32.
-    static const int PACKETDEMOD_CHASE_MAX = 12;
+    static constexpr int PACKETDEMOD_CHASE_MAX = 12;
 
     // Returns true if the frame was accepted - the caller's deduplication decides, and the
     // framer reports that back so callers can count distinct packets rather than the
